/**
 * The English this application keeps until the catalog world `w.lang.en` has it (src/lang/en.mjs reads these facts after the catalog's, in the catalog's format). Hand-maintained; every entry is a question for the
 * knowledge repository (questions.md "w.lang.en vs the hand-over") and goes when the catalog publishes it:
 *   frames     the argument frames added after the import of w.lang.en (source psys2 78f45863): the docs.editor sets (acts.text, 27) and the facts-by-lookup set (acts.facts, 7), and the 5 frames of the act `own`
 *              (the readers of a world's own sentences: they say nothing of English, the import left them out). A frame keeps its `pattern` as written (a catalog frame has `w.lang.en.part` wires instead);
 *              `after=<frame>` puts it behind that frame of its set (the order of the frames is the order of the generated patterns).
 *   joiners    `keep`: words after `and` that continue the noun phrase before it ("Highlight Romania and its neighbours"): the splitter, the card cutter and the one-anaphora check do not cut there.
 *   facts      the acts.facts frames of the map (ask.* over any attribute or relation of a place, layer.* for highlights, pins and lines).
 *   fn         `w.lang.en.fn` (view face): words a request skips when it reads the parts of a face ("please make the hair red", "I want it with a hat"): the catalog has determiners, pronouns and auxiliaries
 *              (read from there by worlds/ui.avatar/facelogic.mjs) but no class of ignorable words: asked of the knowledge repository (politeness, desire, filler, conjunction and preposition words).
 *   neg        `w.lang.en.neg` words of negation and removal the catalog does not list (it has "not" and "dont"): no, without, never, lose, minus: asked of the knowledge repository.
 * Browser-safe: no `node:*`.
 */
